[test-assertion] [test-assertion] Test 'test_a_child_that_is_not_a_group_leader_is_killed_alone' asserts that killpg is not called and that elapsed time is bounded, but does not explicitly assert that proc.terminate() was invoked. The elapsed-time bound implies it, but an explicit assertion would make the test more specific and guard against regressions where the fallback path is skipped.
[test-assertion] [test-assertion] Test 'test_a_refused_group_kill_still_kills_the_child' asserts elapsed time < 10, which implies the child was killed, but does not assert that proc.kill() was called on the fallback path. Adding an assertion on the mock (e.g., via patching subprocess.Popen.kill) would make the intent explicit and verify the fallback branch is actually exercised.
[test-assertion] [test-assertion] Test 'test_output_does_not_accumulate_in_the_parent' uses resource.getrusage, which is not available on Windows. If the test suite is intended to run on Windows, this will error. Consider guarding with sys.platform or using a cross-platform memory measurement approach.
[test-assertion] [test-assertion] The early-return branch in _kill_process_group (when proc.poll() is not None) is not covered by any test. Adding a test that constructs a mock with poll() returning a non-None value would verify this short-circuit path.
